---
import ContentContainer from "../layouts/ContentContainer.astro";
---

<div>
	<section class="border-b border-line">
		<ContentContainer>
			<a
				href="/services"
				class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[.14em] text-muted uppercase hover:text-ink"
				>← All services</a
			>
			<p class="mt-16 eyebrow">Managed IT</p>
			<h1
				class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-5xl font-semibold leading-[.96] tracking-[-.065em] sm:text-7xl"
			>
				Managed IT support
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-8 text-muted">
				Calmer, more dependable technology operations for your team.
			</p>
		</ContentContainer>
	</section>
	<section
		class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_20rem] lg:gap-24 lg:px-12"
	>
		<div class="max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted rich-text">
			<h2 class="text-3xl mb-3">Dependable day-to-day operations</h2>
			<p class="font-medium">
				A practical managed IT partnership keeps core technology reliable
				without requiring your team to coordinate every routine task. The scope
				is agreed in advance and may include user support, endpoint and device
				administration, network and cloud service oversight, account management,
				backups, and vendor coordination. Responsibilities, supported systems,
				escalation paths, and business priorities are documented so both sides
				know what is covered and when project work or specialist assistance is
				handled separately.
			</p>
			<p class="font-medium mt-6">
				Monitoring provides visibility into system health, capacity,
				connectivity, backup results, and other conditions that can affect
				availability. The IT partner reviews alerts, investigates recurring
				issues, and maintains an actionable record of incidents and changes.
				Responsive support combines a clear intake process with practical
				troubleshooting, communication with affected users, and escalation when
				an issue requires a deeper technical or vendor-level response.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted rich-text">
			<h2 class="text-3xl mb-3">Maintenance with security in mind</h2>
			<p class="font-medium">
				Ongoing maintenance includes planned patching, software and firmware
				updates, device configuration, lifecycle planning, and removal of
				obsolete or unnecessary access. Security operations can include endpoint
				protection, multi-factor authentication support, permissions reviews,
				backup validation, vulnerability follow-up, and logging appropriate to
				the environment. These controls should be aligned with the
				organization's systems and risk profile rather than treated as a
				one-time setup.
			</p>
			<p class="font-medium mt-6">
				The partnership should also include regular service reviews. Reviewing
				incidents, monitoring trends, backup status, open risks, and upcoming
				technology changes helps turn support activity into a manageable
				operating plan. This creates a stable foundation for growth while
				keeping expectations clear about what the managed service covers, what
				requires a separate project, and how decisions are made when priorities
				or business requirements change.
			</p>
		</div>
		<aside class="h-fit border-t border-line pt-5 lg:sticky lg:top-8">
			<h2 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[.14em] text-bright uppercase">
				Capabilities
			</h2>
			<ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted">
				<li class="border-b border-line pb-3">Cloud infrastructure</li>
				<li class="border-b border-line pb-3">Monitoring & support</li>
				<li class="border-b border-line pb-3">Security hardening</li>
				<li class="border-b border-line pb-3">Ongoing optimization</li>
			</ul>
		</aside>
	</section>
</div>
